+The first page prints **0850** for the tactical-net request, followed by separate **0920** rows for the NMCC notification and the primary-net request. The handwritten bracket links those latter rows and labels the notification “by primary net.” The typed line still says the primary net was **requested**. The separate **0924** row describes an FAA regional operations center report about American 77 disappearing from radar. The forms give a potential source for the later public 09:20 line description. The document leaves the timing of an actual connection, duration of military participation, and receipt of a specific aircraft report open. The handwriting’s author and date remain open. [AWA-612, physical p. 1](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7598466) · [Prior 09:20 source comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/f425336303bbad671cb6943ff69941d4148b1aeb/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-ada30-layout-2026-11-05/README.md)
 
